<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#registrationLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#CorrectionNotice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A ripe:CorrectionNotice is a fabio:Correction and ripe:IntegrityAssessmentEvidence representing a formal correction notice about a work and used as evidence in a ripe:ResearchIntegrityAssessment. For example, an erratum correcting a published article is a ripe:CorrectionNotice."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#concerns> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "concerns"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#PublicationDetails> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Publication details"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-05-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#HumanReviewer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#Work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A ripe:Work is a fabio:Work and prov:Entity representing a work relevant to a ripe:ResearchIntegrityAssessment. It may be the subject of an assessment, a cited publication, or another work connected to assessment evidence, such as an article associated with a publication notice. For example, an article, a cited paper, or an article retracted by a notice may be represented as a ripe:Work."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ripe/ripe-o#StudyDesignEvidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
